## Spell's built-in dimensions:  each kind of measure, its units, and how they convert
// Built into spell (epic `language` P23, Owen's C5):  compiled once, into the core (`yarn core:gen:templates`).
// A program declares its own the same way:  `data size is a dimension:`, then its units.
// Each unit is said in a unit named above it;  its first `aka` is how a measure in it is written:  `172 cm`.

length is a dimension:
	- its base is "meter", aka "m", aka "meters", aka "metre", aka "metres"
	- one "kilometer", aka "km", aka "kilometers", aka "kilometre", aka "kilometres", is 1000 m
	- one "centimeter", aka "cm", aka "centimeters", aka "centimetre", aka "centimetres", is 1/100 m
	- one "millimeter", aka "mm", aka "millimeters", aka "millimetre", aka "millimetres", is 1/1000 m
	- one "inch", aka "in", aka "\"", aka "inches", is 2.54 cm
	- one "foot", aka "ft", aka "'", aka "feet", is 12 in
	- one "yard", aka "yd", aka "yards", is 3 ft
	- one "mile", aka "mi", aka "miles", is 1760 yd

weight is a dimension:
	- its base is "kilogram", aka "kg", aka "kilograms", aka "kilo", aka "kilos"
	- one "gram", aka "g", aka "grams", is 1/1000 kg
	- one "pound", aka "lb", aka "lbs", aka "pounds", is 0.45359237 kg
	- one "ounce", aka "oz", aka "ounces", is 1/16 lb
	- one "stone", aka "st", aka "stones", is 14 lb

// temperature doesn't start at the same place in each unit:  32 °F is 0 °C
temperature is a dimension:
	- its base is "celsius", aka "°C", aka "degrees celsius"
	- one "fahrenheit", aka "°F", aka "degrees fahrenheit", is 5/9 °C, starting at 32
	- one "kelvin", aka "K", aka "kelvins", is 1 °C, starting at 273.15

volume is a dimension:
	- its base is "liter", aka "l", aka "liters", aka "litre", aka "litres"
	- one "milliliter", aka "ml", aka "milliliters", aka "millilitre", aka "millilitres", is 1/1000 l
	- one "gallon", aka "gal", aka "gallons", is 3.785411784 l
	- one "quart", aka "qt", aka "quarts", is 1/4 gal
	- one "pint", aka "pt", aka "pints", is 1/2 qt
	- one "cup", aka "cup", aka "cups", is 1/2 pt
	- one "fluid ounce", aka "fl oz", aka "fluid ounces", is 1/8 cup
	- one "tablespoon", aka "tbsp", aka "tablespoons", is 1/2 fl oz
	- one "teaspoon", aka "tsp", aka "teaspoons", is 1/3 tbsp

speed is a dimension:
	- its base is "meter per second", aka "m/s", aka "meters per second"
	- one "kilometer per hour", aka "km/h", aka "kilometers per hour", is 1/3.6 m/s
	- one "mile per hour", aka "mph", aka "miles per hour", is 0.44704 m/s
	- one "knot", aka "kn", aka "knots", is 1852/3600 m/s

// a part of a whole, as people write it:  18% is 18 hundredths
// a percent is KEPT as its fraction, 0.18, so `the bill * 18%` is 18% of the bill;  it's shown with its % sign
proportion is a dimension:
	- its base is "fraction", aka "fractions"
	- one "percent", aka "%", aka "per cent", is 1/100 fraction
